WEBVTT

01:35.245 --> 01:37.155
Time to get up, man.

01:38.999 --> 01:41.289
- All right, Dad.
- Come on.

02:49.152 --> 02:50.992
Should be here soon.

03:38.368 --> 03:40.658
- I think I should make a list.
- What do you mean?

03:40.870 --> 03:43.250
- For your birthday gifts?
- Yeah.

03:43.456 --> 03:46.006
You know you're only getting
a couple of things, right?

03:46.209 --> 03:50.259
Yeah, I know. Just to look at
and study so I can choose better.

03:50.463 --> 03:53.383
Okay, well, that's smart.
Yeah, make a list.

03:53.883 --> 03:55.803
Can you spell everything
you're thinking of?

03:56.052 --> 03:59.602
- I think so.
- All right. That's good.

04:03.560 --> 04:06.440
- How you doing in here, man?
- Okay.

04:13.737 --> 04:16.657
Can we go to the park today, after?

04:17.490 --> 04:20.910
No, I gotta go to Oakland.
Well, maybe, we'll see.

04:21.161 --> 04:22.701
Give me a kiss.

04:23.580 --> 04:25.460
I'll talk to you later.

04:28.919 --> 04:30.549
Excuse me.

04:31.338 --> 04:33.048
Oh, excuse me...

04:33.256 --> 04:35.546
...when is somebody
gonna clean this off?

04:38.595 --> 04:41.095
And the Y?
The Y. We talked about this.

04:41.348 --> 04:44.728
It's an I in "happiness."
There's no Y in "happiness." It's an I.

04:47.020 --> 04:48.900
<i>I'm Chris Gardner.</i>

04:49.356 --> 04:52.396
<i>I met my father for the first time</i>
<i>when I was 28 years old.</i>

04:53.193 --> 04:54.863
<i>And I made up my mind</i>
<i>as a young kid...</i>

04:55.111 --> 04:56.571
<i>... that when I had children...</i>

04:56.780 --> 05:00.120
<i>... my children were gonna know</i>
<i>who their father was.</i>

05:01.993 --> 05:04.753
<i>This is part of my life story.</i>

05:05.580 --> 05:08.920
<i>This part is called "Riding the Bus."</i>

05:15.465 --> 05:17.085
What's that?

05:17.717 --> 05:19.927
It's a time machine, isn't it?

05:20.720 --> 05:22.310
Seems like a time machine.

05:22.555 --> 05:25.595
That seems like a time machine.
It's a time machine. Take me with you.

05:25.850 --> 05:27.020
<i>This machine...</i>

05:27.477 --> 05:28.727
<i>... this machine on my lap...</i>

05:28.979 --> 05:30.899
This guy, he has a time machine.

05:31.147 --> 05:34.147
He travels in the past
with this machine and...

05:34.401 --> 05:36.611
- <i>it is not a time machine.</i>

05:37.153 --> 05:39.783
<i>It's a portable</i>
<i>bone-density scanner.</i>

05:40.657 --> 05:43.237
<i>A medical device I sell for a living.</i>

05:43.493 --> 05:45.953
Thank you for the opportunity
to discuss it with you.

05:46.162 --> 05:48.252
- I appreciate it.
- We just don't need it, Chris.

05:48.498 --> 05:50.208
It's unnecessary and expensive.

05:50.417 --> 05:52.537
- Well, maybe next...
- Thank you.

05:53.670 --> 05:58.720
<i>It gave a slightly denser picture</i>
<i>than an x-ray for twice the money.</i>

06:01.761 --> 06:03.311
- Hey.
- Hey, baby.

06:03.513 --> 06:05.183
- What happened?
- No, nothing.

06:05.432 --> 06:06.982
Look, I can't get Christopher today.

06:07.517 --> 06:09.687
Oh, no, you don't, Chris.
I'm back on at 7.

06:09.936 --> 06:11.646
I know. I have got to go to Oakland.

06:12.105 --> 06:14.975
So I gotta get Christopher home,
feed him, bathe him...

06:15.191 --> 06:17.821
...get him in bed,
and be back here by 7?

06:18.028 --> 06:20.158
- Yes.
- And we got the tax-bill notice today.

06:20.363 --> 06:23.873
- What are you gonna do about that?
- Look, this is what we gotta do.

06:28.204 --> 06:32.384
<i>You see that car? The one</i>
<i>with the pretty yellow shoe on it?</i>

06:32.626 --> 06:33.956
<i>That's mine.</i>

06:34.210 --> 06:36.130
<i>There's no parking near hospitals.</i>

06:36.379 --> 06:38.839
<i>That's what happens</i>
<i>when you're always in a rush.</i>

06:39.049 --> 06:40.929
Thanks anyway. Very much.

06:41.134 --> 06:44.054
- Maybe next quarter.
- It's possible.

06:44.971 --> 06:50.481
<i>I needed to sell at least two scanners</i>
<i>a month for rent and daycare.</i>

06:51.394 --> 06:52.694
<i>I'd have to sell one more...</i>

06:52.896 --> 06:56.686
<i>... to pay off all of those tickets</i>
<i>under my windshield wiper.</i>

07:03.490 --> 07:05.490
<i>The problem is...</i>

07:06.409 --> 07:08.869
<i>... I haven't sold any for a while.</i>

07:10.580 --> 07:13.250
Since when do you not like
macaroni and cheese?

07:13.500 --> 07:16.000
Since birth?

07:18.505 --> 07:20.505
- What's that?
- What?

07:20.757 --> 07:23.797
- What is this?
- It's a gift for Christopher.

07:24.010 --> 07:26.510
- From who?
- Cynthia from work.

07:26.763 --> 07:29.813
It's for adults. Chris can't use it.
She didn't know.

07:30.016 --> 07:32.016
What are you supposed
to do with it?

07:32.769 --> 07:35.809
Make every side the same colour.

07:37.107 --> 07:39.397
Did you pay the taxes?

07:39.693 --> 07:42.823
No, I'm gonna
have to file an extension.

07:43.613 --> 07:47.743
- You already filed an extension.
- Yeah, well, I gotta file another one.

07:48.118 --> 07:51.828
That's... It's $650.
I'll have it in the next month.

07:52.372 --> 07:54.172
That means interest, right?

07:54.374 --> 07:56.754
- And a penalty?
- Yeah, a little bit.

07:56.960 --> 08:02.590
Look, why don't you let me do this?
All right, just relax. Okay?

08:02.799 --> 08:06.929
- Come here. Calm down.
- I have to go back to work.

08:14.978 --> 08:18.608
Let's get ready for bed.
Hey, put your plate in the sink.

08:19.316 --> 08:22.236
<i>A few days ago I was presented</i>
<i>with a report I'd asked for...</i>

08:22.485 --> 08:26.155
<i>... a comprehensive audit, if you will,</i>
<i>of our economic condition.</i>

08:26.823 --> 08:29.583
<i>You won't like it. I didn't like it.</i>

08:29.826 --> 08:31.446
<i>But we have to face the truth...</i>

08:31.661 --> 08:34.291
<i>... and then go to work</i>
<i>to turn things around.</i>

08:34.497 --> 08:38.247
<i>And make no mistake about it,</i>
<i>we can turn them around.</i>

08:38.501 --> 08:41.551
<i>The federal budget is out of control.</i>

08:41.755 --> 08:45.125
<i>And we face runaway deficits</i>
<i>of almost $80 billion...</i>

08:45.342 --> 08:48.762
<i>... for this budget year</i>
<i>that ends September 30th.</i>

08:49.012 --> 08:54.182
<i>That deficit is larger than</i>
<i>the entire federal budget in 1957.</i>

08:54.434 --> 08:56.984
<i>And so is the almost $80 billion...</i>

08:57.187 --> 09:01.477
<i>... we will pay in interest</i>
<i>this year on the national debt.</i>

09:02.108 --> 09:04.648
<i>Twenty years ago, in 1960...</i>

09:04.861 --> 09:08.991
<i>... our federal government payroll</i>
<i>was less than $13 billion.</i>

09:09.199 --> 09:11.909
<i>Today it is 75 billion.</i>

09:12.118 --> 09:17.668
<i>During these 20 years, our population</i>
<i>has only increased by 23.3 percent...</i>

09:35.892 --> 09:38.602
Man, I got two questions for you:

09:38.853 --> 09:41.943
What do you do?
And how do you do it?

09:43.441 --> 09:46.531
- I'm a stockbroker.
- Stockbroker. Oh, goodness.

09:46.736 --> 09:48.696
Had to go to college
to be a stockbroker, huh?

09:48.989 --> 09:52.699
You don't have to. Have to be good
with numbers and good with people.

09:52.909 --> 09:55.289
- That's it.
- Hey, you take care.

09:55.537 --> 09:57.537
I'll let you hang on to my car
for the weekend.

09:57.747 --> 10:00.207
- But I need it back for Monday.
- Feed the meter.

10:07.424 --> 10:09.804
<i>I still remember that moment.</i>

10:14.097 --> 10:18.727
<i>They all looked</i>
<i>so damn happy to me.</i>

10:25.942 --> 10:28.322
<i>Why couldn't I look like that?</i>

10:45.962 --> 10:47.262
I'm gonna try to get home by 6.

10:47.464 --> 10:50.594
I'm gonna stop by a brokerage firm
after work.

10:50.800 --> 10:54.100
- For what?
- I wanna see about a job there.

10:54.304 --> 10:56.934
Yeah? What job?

10:57.474 --> 10:59.434
You know, when I...

10:59.643 --> 11:02.273
When I was a kid, I could go through
a math book in a week.

11:02.479 --> 11:05.819
So I'm gonna go see about
what job they got down there.

11:06.983 --> 11:08.863
What job?

11:11.821 --> 11:13.571
Stockbroker.

11:15.909 --> 11:19.079
- Stockbroker?
- Yeah.

11:19.537 --> 11:21.457
Not an astronaut?

11:38.515 --> 11:39.975
Don't talk to me like that, Linda.

11:41.101 --> 11:44.901
I'm gonna go down and see about this,
and I'm gonna do it during the day.

11:45.105 --> 11:46.815
You should probably
do your sales calls.

11:47.274 --> 11:49.694
I don't need you to tell me
about my sales calls, Linda.

11:49.943 --> 11:53.113
I got three of them
before the damn office is even open.

11:53.697 --> 11:56.067
Do you remember
that rent is due next week?

11:56.283 --> 11:58.163
Probably not.

11:58.785 --> 12:00.825
We're already two months behind.

12:01.037 --> 12:04.077
Next week we'll owe three months.

12:04.541 --> 12:08.671
I've been pulling double shifts
for four months now, Chris.

12:09.129 --> 12:13.379
Just sell what's in your contract.
Get us out of that business.

12:13.633 --> 12:17.303
Linda, that is what I am trying to do.

12:18.054 --> 12:20.724
This is what I'm trying to do
for my family...

12:20.974 --> 12:22.314
...for you and for Christopher.

12:23.727 --> 12:25.847
What's the matter with you?

12:30.066 --> 12:31.686
Linda.

12:32.319 --> 12:33.819
Linda.

13:00.847 --> 13:05.887
<i>This part of my life</i>
<i>is called "Being Stupid."</i>

13:07.938 --> 13:09.228
Can I ask you a favour, miss?

13:09.439 --> 13:13.319
Do you mind if I leave this here
with you just for five minutes?

13:13.526 --> 13:16.026
I have a meeting in there
and I don't wanna carry that...

13:16.279 --> 13:18.239
...looking smalltime.

13:19.115 --> 13:23.535
Here is a dollar and I'll give you
more money when I come back out.

13:23.787 --> 13:26.997
Okay? It's not valuable.
You can't sell it anywhere.

13:27.958 --> 13:33.088
I can't even sell it, and it's my job.
All right? Be right back.

13:39.803 --> 13:42.143
- Chris? Tim Brophy, Resources.
- Yes. How are you?

13:42.389 --> 13:43.679
- Follow me.
- Yes, sir.

13:43.890 --> 13:46.640
Let me see if I can find you
an application for our internship.

13:46.893 --> 13:50.113
I'm afraid that's all we can do for you.
See, this is a satellite office.

13:50.313 --> 13:52.943
Jay Twistle in the main office,
he oversees Witter Resources.

13:53.149 --> 13:55.279
I mean, I'm... You know,
I'm just this office.

13:55.485 --> 13:58.405
As you can see, we got a hell of lot
of applications here, so...

13:58.655 --> 14:01.615
Normally I have a résumé sheet,
but I can't seem to find it anywhere.

14:01.825 --> 14:05.245
- <i>We...</i>
- Thank you very much.

14:05.495 --> 14:06.615
I need to go.

14:07.247 --> 14:08.917
I'll bring this back.

14:09.165 --> 14:12.285
- Thank you.
- Okay.

14:18.675 --> 14:23.135
<i>Trusting a hippie girl with my scanner.</i>
<i>Why did I do that?</i>

14:23.346 --> 14:24.966
Excuse me. Excuse me.

14:25.181 --> 14:30.651
<i>Like I said, this part of my life</i>
<i>is called "Being Stupid."</i>

14:33.857 --> 14:38.527
Hey! Hey! Hey! Don't move!
Don't move! Stay...!

14:46.536 --> 14:48.826
Stop! Stop!

14:49.039 --> 14:52.249
Don't move!
Stop this...! Stop the train!

14:53.293 --> 14:55.593
Stop! Stop!

15:10.560 --> 15:14.230
<i>The programme took just 20 people</i>
<i>every six months.</i>

15:14.481 --> 15:16.521
<i>One got the job.</i>

15:18.068 --> 15:23.448
<i>There were three blank lines after</i>
<i>"high school" to list more education.</i>

15:24.991 --> 15:27.791
<i>I didn't need that many lines.</i>

15:32.916 --> 15:35.876
Try and sleep. It's late.

15:45.845 --> 15:49.425
<i>It's a puzzle measuring just 3 inches</i>
<i>by 3 inches on each side...</i>

15:49.683 --> 15:52.063
<i>... made up of multiple colours</i>
<i>that you twist and turn...</i>

15:52.269 --> 15:54.899
<i>... and try to get</i>
<i>to a solid colour on each side.</i>

15:55.105 --> 15:58.725
<i>This little cube</i>
<i>is the gift sensation of 1981.</i>

15:58.942 --> 16:00.322
<i>Don't expect to solve it easily.</i>

16:00.527 --> 16:02.947
<i>Although we did encounter</i>
<i>one math professor at USF...</i>

16:03.196 --> 16:05.656
<i>... who took just 30 minutes on his.</i>

16:05.865 --> 16:08.075
<i>This is as far as I've gotten</i>
<i>on mine.</i>

16:08.285 --> 16:11.655
<i>As you can see,</i>
<i>I still have a long way to go.</i>

16:11.871 --> 16:14.501
<i>This is Jim Finnerty reporting</i>
<i>for KJSF in Richmond.</i>

16:14.708 --> 16:17.418
Hey, wake up.

16:17.627 --> 16:19.127
Eat.

16:20.297 --> 16:22.717
- Bye, Mom.
- Bye, baby.

16:22.966 --> 16:25.926
- Come back without that, please.
- Oh, yeah, I'm going to.

16:26.136 --> 16:29.056
So go ahead, say goodbye to it,
because I'm coming back without it.

16:29.306 --> 16:31.676
Goodbye and good riddance.

16:31.891 --> 16:33.851
You ain't had to add
the "good riddance" part.

16:34.060 --> 16:35.100
Bye, Mom.

16:36.646 --> 16:37.976
Bye.

16:38.231 --> 16:41.781
It's written as P-P-Y, but it's
supposed to be an I in "happiness."

16:41.985 --> 16:45.105
- Is it an adjective?
- No, actually it's a noun.

16:45.322 --> 16:47.072
But it's not spelled right.

16:47.324 --> 16:50.874
- Is "fuck" spelled right?
- Yeah, that's spelled right.

16:51.077 --> 16:54.207
But that's not part of the motto,
so you're not supposed to learn that.

16:54.414 --> 16:59.294
That's an adult word to show anger
and other things.

16:59.502 --> 17:02.382
- But just don't use that one, okay?
- Okay.

17:02.589 --> 17:04.759
What's that say
on the back of your bag?

17:05.091 --> 17:07.051
My nickname.

17:07.260 --> 17:08.850
We pick nicknames.

17:09.095 --> 17:12.425
- Oh, yeah? What's it say?
- "Hot Rod."

17:15.435 --> 17:17.475
- Did you have a nickname?
- Yep.

17:17.687 --> 17:20.397
- What?
- "Ten-Gallon Head."

17:20.607 --> 17:23.487
- What's that?
- I grew up in Louisiana, near Texas.

17:23.693 --> 17:28.323
Everybody wears cowboy hats.
And a ten-gallon's a big hat.

17:28.531 --> 17:32.121
I was smart back then,
so they called me Ten-Gallon Head.

17:32.702 --> 17:34.832
- Hoss wears that hat.
- Hoss?

17:35.121 --> 17:36.831
Hoss Cartwright on <i>Bonanza.</i>

17:37.290 --> 17:40.840
- How do you know <i>Bonanza?</i>
- We watch it at Mrs. Chu's.

17:41.544 --> 17:44.594
- You watch <i>Bonanza</i> at daycare?
- Yeah.

17:45.715 --> 17:47.715
When? When do you watch it?

17:47.968 --> 17:51.598
- After snack? After your nap?
- After <i>Love Boat.</i>

17:56.559 --> 17:58.689
I made my list for my birthday.

17:59.479 --> 18:03.979
- Yeah, what'd you put on there?
- A basketball or an ant farm.

18:07.571 --> 18:11.871
- He says he's been watching TV.
- Oh, little TV for history.

18:12.075 --> 18:15.155
- <i>Love Boat?</i>
- For history. Navy.

18:15.912 --> 18:17.622
That's not the Navy.

18:17.831 --> 18:19.961
I mean, he could
watch television at home.

18:20.166 --> 18:24.546
We're paying you $150 a month.
If he's gonna be sitting around...

18:24.796 --> 18:27.126
...watching TV all day,
we're taking him out of here.

18:27.340 --> 18:31.140
Go pay more at other daycare
if you don't like Navy TV.

18:33.013 --> 18:38.233
You late pay anyway.
You complain. I complain.

18:39.769 --> 18:43.519
Can you at least put the dog upstairs
in your room or something?

18:43.773 --> 18:45.193
Bye.

19:29.569 --> 19:33.449
<i>I was waiting for</i>
<i>Witter Resource head Jay Twistle...</i>

19:33.740 --> 19:39.200
<i>... whose name sounded so delightful,</i>
<i>like he’d give me a job and a hug.</i>

19:39.412 --> 19:43.422
<i>I just had to show him I was good</i>
<i>with numbers and good with people.</i>

19:43.625 --> 19:45.165
- Morning, Mr. Twistle.
- Good morning.

19:45.418 --> 19:46.798
- Mr. Twistle, Chris Gardner.
- Hi.

19:47.045 --> 19:49.795
I wanted to drop this off personally
and make your acquaintance.

19:50.006 --> 19:53.386
I thought I'd catch you on the way in.
I'd love the opportunity to discuss...

19:53.593 --> 19:55.803
...what may seem like weaknesses
on my application.

19:56.012 --> 19:58.812
We'll start with this, and we'll call you
if we wanna sit down.

19:59.015 --> 20:01.975
- Yes, sir. You have a great day.
- You too.

20:09.067 --> 20:10.647
<i>Hey, yeah, how you doing?</i>

20:10.860 --> 20:13.030
This is Chris Gardner calling
for Dr. Delsey.

20:13.280 --> 20:15.410
Yeah, I'm running a little late
for a sales call.

20:15.615 --> 20:19.115
I was wondering if...
Yeah, Osteo National.

20:19.369 --> 20:21.869
Right. We can still...? Half an hour?

20:22.080 --> 20:25.750
Yes. Beautiful. Beautiful.
Thank you, thank you.

20:35.302 --> 20:38.432
Hey! Hey!

20:39.556 --> 20:40.886
Hey!

20:41.099 --> 20:42.479
<i>This part of my life...</i>

20:42.726 --> 20:45.396
- Wait!
- <i>... this part here...</i>

20:46.980 --> 20:48.570
<i>... it's called "Running."</i>

20:48.815 --> 20:50.685
Hey! Hey!

20:50.901 --> 20:52.491
Wait!

20:53.403 --> 20:56.203
Hey! Wait!

20:56.406 --> 20:58.776
<i>That was my stolen machine.</i>

20:58.992 --> 21:01.042
<i>Unless she was with</i>
<i>a guy who sold them too.</i>

21:02.579 --> 21:03.829
<i>Which was unlikely...</i>

21:04.039 --> 21:06.749
<i>... because I was the only one</i>
<i>selling them in the Bay Area.</i>

21:06.917 --> 21:09.537
<i>I spent our entire life savings</i>
<i>on these things.</i>

21:12.005 --> 21:15.545
<i>It was such</i>
<i>a revolutionary machine.</i>

21:16.760 --> 21:18.140
- Can you feel it, baby?
- Oh, yeah.

21:18.345 --> 21:19.885
You got me doing all the work.

21:20.096 --> 21:22.596
<i>What I didn't know</i>
<i>is that doctors and hospitals...</i>

21:22.807 --> 21:26.687
<i>... would consider them</i>
<i>unnecessary luxuries.</i>

21:29.356 --> 21:32.726
<i>I even asked the landlord</i>
<i>to take a picture.</i>

21:34.027 --> 21:38.907
<i>So if I lost one, it was like losing</i>
<i>a month's groceries.</i>

21:41.868 --> 21:44.788
Hey, hey! Wait! Wait!

21:47.707 --> 21:50.377
Hey, get back here!

21:54.965 --> 21:57.425
Hey, man, I...

21:59.302 --> 22:01.602
- Who's he?
- He's that guy...

22:12.148 --> 22:15.988
- Did you forget?
- Forget what?

22:16.987 --> 22:19.447
You're not supposed
to have any of those.

22:19.656 --> 22:22.866
- Yeah, I know.
- You have two now.

22:33.253 --> 22:34.803
Hey.

22:37.757 --> 22:39.337
Hey, Mom.

22:44.681 --> 22:48.561
One, two, three!

22:49.686 --> 22:52.766
- That's a basketball!
- Hey, hey. What do you mean?

22:53.023 --> 22:54.693
You don't know that
that's a basketball.

22:54.941 --> 22:58.821
This could be an ant farm. This could
be a microscope or anything.

22:59.029 --> 23:01.489
- No, it's not.
- There, there.

23:01.948 --> 23:04.988
All right, come on.
Open him up. Open him up.

23:10.874 --> 23:15.254
- That paper's a little heavy, huh?
- Yeah, but I got it.

23:26.473 --> 23:29.023
You should've seen me
out there today.

23:29.226 --> 23:31.766
Somebody stole a scanner.
I had to run the old girl down...

23:31.978 --> 23:33.558
Whatever.

23:35.148 --> 23:38.238
- What?
- Whatever, Chris.

23:38.818 --> 23:40.648
What the hell
you got attitude about?

23:40.904 --> 23:43.664
- "Whatever" what?
- Every day's got some damn story.

23:43.907 --> 23:45.197
Hey, Roy. Roy!

23:45.408 --> 23:47.698
Can you beat your little rug
when nobody's out here?

23:47.911 --> 23:49.371
There's dust and shit all over.

23:49.579 --> 23:51.959
- I'm trying to keep a clean house.
- Hey, wait a second.

23:52.165 --> 23:54.915
Look, Linda, relax.

23:55.168 --> 23:58.458
We're gonna come out of this.
Everything is gonna be fine, all right?

23:59.589 --> 24:03.469
You said that before,
when I got pregnant. "It'll be fine."

24:03.677 --> 24:08.677
- So you don't trust me now?
- Whatever. I don't care.

24:23.863 --> 24:26.073
- Taxi!
- Mr. Twistle.

24:26.283 --> 24:28.953
- Yeah, hi.
- Hi. Chris Gardner.

24:29.202 --> 24:31.002
Yeah, hi. Listen.
What can I do for you?

24:31.204 --> 24:34.254
I submitted an application for the
intern programme about a month ago...

24:34.457 --> 24:36.707
...and I would just love
to sit with you briefly...

24:36.960 --> 24:38.880
Listen, I'm going
to Noe Valley, Chris.

24:39.129 --> 24:42.379
- Take care of yourself.
- Mr. Twistle.

24:42.632 --> 24:44.932
Actually, I'm on my way
to Noe Valley also.

24:45.135 --> 24:46.885
How about we share a ride?

24:48.388 --> 24:50.558
- All right, get in.
- All right.

24:56.646 --> 24:59.396
So when I was in the Navy,
I worked for a doctor...

24:59.649 --> 25:02.439
...who loved to play golf,
hours every day...

25:02.652 --> 25:07.282
...and I would actually
perform medical procedures...

25:07.490 --> 25:09.030
...when he'd leave me in the office.

25:09.242 --> 25:14.502
So I'm used to being in a position
where I have to make decisions and...

25:15.999 --> 25:18.789
Mr. Twistle, listen.
This is a very important...

25:19.002 --> 25:21.212
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
This thing's impossible.

25:23.340 --> 25:25.430
- I can do it.
- No, you can't. No one can.

25:25.675 --> 25:28.345
- That's bullshit.
- No, I'm pretty sure I can do it.

25:28.762 --> 25:31.932
- No, you can't.
- Let me see it.

25:32.515 --> 25:33.725
Give it here.

25:36.686 --> 25:40.976
Oh, yeah. Oh, wow,
you really messed it up.

25:41.191 --> 25:42.731
Sorry.

25:43.276 --> 25:49.236
It looks like it works around a swivel,
so the centre pieces never move.

25:49.449 --> 25:52.539
So if it's yellow in the centre,
that's the yellow side.

25:52.786 --> 25:55.246
If it's red in the centre,
that's the red side.

25:55.455 --> 25:59.075
- Okay.
- So... You can slow down.

25:59.292 --> 26:02.342
Listen, we can drive around all day.
I don't believe you can do this.

26:02.545 --> 26:04.255
- Yeah, I can.
- No, you can't.

26:04.464 --> 26:05.634
- Yes, I can.
- No, you can't.

26:05.882 --> 26:07.762
I'm telling you, no one can.

26:09.719 --> 26:11.929
See? That's all I ever do.

26:24.818 --> 26:27.108
You almost have this side.

26:27.737 --> 26:29.197
Holy cow.

26:39.416 --> 26:43.206
- You almost had that one.
- I'm gonna get it.

26:50.760 --> 26:52.510
Look at that.

27:15.785 --> 27:16.995
You're almost there.

27:40.727 --> 27:44.437
- 1710.
- This is me.

27:46.566 --> 27:47.936
Good job.

27:49.819 --> 27:52.909
- Goodbye.
- Yeah. I'll see you soon.

27:55.325 --> 27:57.035
Where are you going, sir?

27:57.244 --> 28:00.254
Excuse me, sir.
Where are you going, please?

28:03.583 --> 28:05.293
Two... A couple of blocks.

28:05.502 --> 28:08.922
- Just flip around.
- Okay.

28:50.880 --> 28:53.590
Hey! Stop it! Hey!

28:53.967 --> 28:55.507
- Where are you going? Come here!
- No!

28:55.719 --> 28:58.559
- No, no, no!
- You asshole, give me my money!

28:58.805 --> 29:00.095
- Give me my money.
- Please stop.

29:00.307 --> 29:02.307
- Please, please, please!
- Son of a bitch.

29:02.559 --> 29:05.059
Please! He should've paid you!

29:05.312 --> 29:06.812
- Come here!
- I'm sorry.

29:07.063 --> 29:08.693
- I'm so sorry.
- I'll kick your ass!

29:09.232 --> 29:12.362
- I'm sorry!
- Idiot.

29:23.163 --> 29:24.503
I'll get you!

29:24.748 --> 29:28.208
I'm going to kill you!
I'm going to kill you!

29:43.600 --> 29:45.690
Hey!

29:45.936 --> 29:48.766
Stop it, you son of a bitch!

29:49.105 --> 29:51.145
Stop him!

29:54.611 --> 29:57.071
Stop him!

30:02.369 --> 30:04.039
<i>The doors are closing.</i>

30:04.287 --> 30:07.077
<i>Please stand clear of the doors.</i>

30:15.048 --> 30:18.128
No! No! No!

30:20.804 --> 30:22.604
No!

30:45.829 --> 30:48.119
- <i>Hello?</i>
- Hey, yeah.

30:48.331 --> 30:50.041
Sorry I couldn't
make it home on time.

30:50.250 --> 30:54.460
- <i>Chris, I missed my shift.</i>
- Yeah, I know. I'm sorry about that.

30:54.671 --> 30:57.971
Look, I'm on my way right now.
Are you all right with Christopher?

30:58.174 --> 31:00.554
<i>I'm leaving. Chris, I'm leaving.</i>

31:00.760 --> 31:02.760
- What?
- <i>Did you hear what I said?</i>

31:03.680 --> 31:07.560
I have my things together,
and I'm taking our son...

31:07.767 --> 31:09.307
...and we're gonna leave now.

31:09.686 --> 31:11.056
<i>I'm gonna put the phone down.</i>

31:11.271 --> 31:14.821
- Linda, wait a minute. Hold it, hold...
- <i>I'm going to leave. We are leaving.</i>

31:20.030 --> 31:23.950
<i>It was right then that I started</i>
<i>thinking about Thomas Jefferson...</i>

31:25.285 --> 31:27.695
<i>... the Declaration of Independence...</i>

31:28.038 --> 31:33.998
<i>... and the part about our right to life,</i>
<i>liberty and the pursuit of happiness.</i>

31:34.210 --> 31:36.050
<i>And I remember thinking.</i>

31:36.296 --> 31:40.626
<i>How did he know</i>
<i>to put the "pursuit" part in there?</i>

31:40.884 --> 31:45.514
<i>That maybe happiness is something</i>
<i>that we can only pursue.</i>

31:45.722 --> 31:48.772
<i>And maybe we can actually</i>
<i>never have it...</i>

31:49.142 --> 31:50.772
<i>... no matter what.</i>

31:50.977 --> 31:52.687
<i>How did he know that?</i>

31:57.901 --> 32:00.701
Linda. Linda.

32:33.687 --> 32:35.357
- Hello?
- <i>Chris.</i>

32:35.605 --> 32:38.185
- Who is this?
- <i>Jay Twistle.</i>

32:39.025 --> 32:40.855
- Hey.
- <i>Dean Witter.</i>

32:41.111 --> 32:43.781
Yeah, of course. How are you?

32:43.947 --> 32:46.407
<i>I'm fine. Listen, do you still</i>
<i>wanna come in and talk?</i>

32:46.616 --> 32:47.906
Yes, sir. Absolutely.

32:48.118 --> 32:50.998
<i>I'll tell you what. Come on by</i>
<i>day after tomorrow, in the morning.</i>

32:51.204 --> 32:54.964
<i>We're interviewing for the internships.</i>
<i>You got a pen and paper?</i>

32:55.208 --> 32:56.748
Yes. Yes, I do.

32:59.713 --> 33:02.473
- Hold on one second.
- <i>All right.</i>

33:06.386 --> 33:08.466
<i>Hello?</i>

33:08.722 --> 33:11.022
- <i>Chris?</i>
- Go ahead. I have one.

33:11.224 --> 33:13.854
<i>Write this number down so you can</i>
<i>call my secretary, Janice.</i>

33:14.060 --> 33:16.100
- <i>She can give you all the specifics.</i>
- Yep.

33:16.313 --> 33:18.193
- <i>Okay, 415.</i>
- 415.

33:18.398 --> 33:20.108
- <i>864.</i>
- 864.

33:20.317 --> 33:22.317
- <i>0256.</i>
- 0256.

33:22.569 --> 33:25.529
- <i>Yeah, extension 4796.</i>
- 4796.

33:25.739 --> 33:29.989
- <i>Right. Call her tomorrow.</i>
- Yes, sir. 415-864-0256.

33:30.243 --> 33:31.493
- <i>Okay, buddy.</i>
- All right, yes.

33:31.745 --> 33:33.865
- Thank you very much.
- <i>We'll see you soon.</i>

33:34.664 --> 33:37.794
864-0256.

33:38.001 --> 33:41.211
4796. Janice.

33:44.257 --> 33:46.087
- Chris.
- Hey.

33:46.343 --> 33:48.553
Did you...? Have you seen
Linda and Christopher?

33:48.762 --> 33:50.642
- No. You catch the game last night?
- No, no.

33:50.847 --> 33:52.217
You didn't see that, 118, 1...?

33:52.432 --> 33:54.642
Excuse me, did Linda
and Christopher come in here?

33:54.851 --> 33:58.481
- No, I haven't seen them.
- 119-120. Double overtime.

33:58.688 --> 34:00.818
Moons hits a three-pointer
at 17 seconds left.

34:01.024 --> 34:02.654
Wayne, Wayne, Wayne.

34:02.859 --> 34:04.989
Can't talk to you
about numbers right now.

34:05.195 --> 34:07.815
- What's your problem with numbers?
- <i>864-2...</i>

34:08.031 --> 34:09.951
- And you owe me money.
- Yeah.

34:10.200 --> 34:11.910
You owe me $14.

34:12.118 --> 34:13.998
I'm gonna get that to you.

34:14.871 --> 34:17.331
I need my money.
I need my money.

34:18.458 --> 34:20.498
Fourteen's a number.

34:46.987 --> 34:50.197
Hey, don't you ever take my son
away from me again.

34:50.407 --> 34:51.697
- You hear me?
- Leave me alone!

34:51.908 --> 34:53.698
Don't take my son away
from me again.

34:53.910 --> 34:55.700
Do you understand
what I'm saying to you?

34:55.912 --> 34:59.212
Don't you walk away from me when
I'm talking to you. Do you hear me?

34:59.416 --> 35:00.916
- Do you wanna leave?
- Yeah.

35:01.167 --> 35:03.957
- You wanna leave?
- Yes, I want to leave!

35:05.255 --> 35:07.045
Get the hell out of here,
then, Linda.

35:07.257 --> 35:09.797
Get the hell out of here.
Christopher's staying with me.

35:10.010 --> 35:12.300
You're the one that dragged
us down. You hear me?

35:12.512 --> 35:15.602
- You are so weak.
- No. I am not happy anymore.

35:15.849 --> 35:18.389
- I'm just not happy!
- Then go get happy, Linda!

35:18.602 --> 35:19.982
Just go get happy.

35:20.520 --> 35:22.400
But Christopher's living with me.

35:22.606 --> 35:24.396
- Stop!
- Did you hear what I said?

35:24.691 --> 35:27.071
Christopher's living with me!

35:53.303 --> 35:56.183
Hey. Come on, let's go.

35:56.389 --> 35:58.729
- How you doing, Mrs. Chu?
- Hi.

36:02.395 --> 36:04.935
- Where's Mom?
- Look, just get your stuff.

36:05.148 --> 36:08.608
But she told me she was
coming to pick me up today.

36:08.818 --> 36:10.858
Yeah, I know.

36:11.988 --> 36:16.618
I talked to Mom earlier.
Everything's fine, okay?

36:22.082 --> 36:24.292
Where do I sleep tonight?

36:24.501 --> 36:26.631
Let me ask you something.
Are you happy?

36:26.836 --> 36:29.456
- Yeah.
- All right. Because I'm happy.

36:29.673 --> 36:33.133
And if you're happy and I'm happy,
then that's a good thing, right?

36:33.343 --> 36:34.893
- Yeah.
- All right.

36:35.136 --> 36:37.136
You're sleeping with me.

36:37.347 --> 36:41.977
You're staying at home,
where you belong, all right?

36:56.491 --> 36:58.121
Christopher.

37:15.719 --> 37:18.509
Hey, listen. I need the rent.

37:18.722 --> 37:20.142
I can't wait anymore.

37:20.390 --> 37:22.730
Yeah, I'm good for that, Charlie.
I'm gonna get it.

37:22.976 --> 37:25.976
Why don't you go two blocks over
at the Mission Inn motel?

37:26.229 --> 37:27.729
It's half what you pay here.

37:27.981 --> 37:31.361
Listen, Chris. I need you out
of here in the morning.

37:32.736 --> 37:34.856
The hell am I supposed
to be out of here tomorrow?

37:35.071 --> 37:36.281
I got painters coming in.

37:36.489 --> 37:38.779
- All right, look. I need more time.
- No.

37:38.992 --> 37:41.122
All right, I'll paint it myself.

37:41.328 --> 37:46.708
All right, but I just... I gotta have some
more time... I got my son up in here.

37:51.588 --> 37:56.378
All right. One week.
And you paint it.

38:48.311 --> 38:49.901
Chris Gardner?

38:50.480 --> 38:53.190
Yeah. What happened?

38:53.400 --> 38:57.280
- Payable to the City of San Francisco.
- Does it have to be the full amount?

38:57.487 --> 39:00.947
You gotta pay each parking ticket,
otherwise, you're staying.

39:01.157 --> 39:02.617
This is all I got.

39:08.164 --> 39:10.834
We verify at 9:30
tomorrow morning.

39:11.334 --> 39:14.384
- What?
- You gotta stay until this thing clears.

39:16.590 --> 39:18.130
No.

39:18.341 --> 39:20.141
No, I can't spend the night here.

39:20.385 --> 39:22.925
- I have to pick up my son.
- We verify at 9:30 tomorrow.

39:23.179 --> 39:27.769
Sir, I have a job interview at Dean
Witter at 10: 15 tomorrow morning.

39:27.976 --> 39:29.636
- I cannot stay...
- 9:30 tomorrow morning.

39:29.853 --> 39:32.193
What am I supposed to do
with my son?

39:32.397 --> 39:34.857
- Is there anyone else who can...?
- I take care of him.

39:35.108 --> 39:38.108
Maybe we can go and have
Social Services pick him up.

39:42.198 --> 39:45.828
All right.
Can I have my phone call, please?

39:49.080 --> 39:51.290
- Hello.
- <i>Hey.</i>

39:51.541 --> 39:53.211
What do you want?

39:54.377 --> 39:59.007
You gotta get Christopher
from daycare. I can't.

40:00.216 --> 40:03.846
Just keep him for the night and I'm...
And... Just one night.

40:04.054 --> 40:06.104
<i>What happened?</i>

40:06.306 --> 40:09.766
I'll pick him up
from daycare tomorrow.

40:09.976 --> 40:11.726
I'm gonna go right...
You can just...

40:11.978 --> 40:14.228
You can drop him off
and I'll pick him up.

40:14.606 --> 40:18.026
- No.
- <i>Come on, Linda.</i>

40:18.276 --> 40:22.486
- <i>Why you doing that?</i>
- No, I wanna take him to the park.

40:22.948 --> 40:27.038
To Golden Gate
after daycare tomorrow.

40:28.328 --> 40:30.408
- How is he?
- He's fine.

40:30.664 --> 40:33.714
All right, just... All right,
take him to the park...

40:33.917 --> 40:37.707
...and bring him back, all right?

40:37.921 --> 40:40.881
All right, just bring me my son back.

40:41.841 --> 40:43.721
<i>Okay?</i>

40:43.927 --> 40:45.467
<i>Linda?</i>

40:45.679 --> 40:47.559
I'll bring him back around 6.

40:49.432 --> 40:51.602
All right, all right.

40:51.851 --> 40:53.691
Thank you.

40:56.106 --> 40:57.606
Bye.

41:22.465 --> 41:24.125
I'm okay?

41:59.085 --> 42:01.205
Excuse me. Excuse me.

42:01.755 --> 42:03.205
Yes, I did.

42:11.848 --> 42:13.638
Mr. Gardner.

42:20.774 --> 42:22.654
This way.

42:24.861 --> 42:26.911
It'll be right over there.

42:39.042 --> 42:40.382
What is the one like that one?

43:02.065 --> 43:03.935
Chris Gardner.

43:06.570 --> 43:08.200
Chris Gardner.

43:08.655 --> 43:10.615
How are you? Good morning.

43:11.241 --> 43:15.081
Chris Gardner. Chris Gardner.
Good to see you again.

43:15.287 --> 43:17.247
Chris Gardner. Pleasure.

43:18.915 --> 43:20.995
I've been sitting there
for the last half-hour...

43:21.251 --> 43:22.751
...trying to come up with a story...

43:23.003 --> 43:27.223
...that would explain my being here
dressed like this.

43:27.424 --> 43:31.474
And I wanted to come up with a story
that would demonstrate qualities...

43:31.678 --> 43:36.518
...that I'm sure you all admire here,
like earnestness or diligence.

43:36.766 --> 43:41.396
Team-playing, something.
And I couldn't think of anything.

43:42.647 --> 43:44.357
So the truth is...

43:44.608 --> 43:47.188
...I was arrested
for failure to pay parking tickets.

43:47.444 --> 43:49.244
Parking tickets?

43:49.779 --> 43:53.329
And I ran all the way here from
the Polk Station, the police station.

43:53.575 --> 43:55.535
What were you doing
before you were arrested?

43:55.785 --> 43:58.745
I was painting my apartment.

43:58.955 --> 44:01.115
Is it dry now?

44:01.917 --> 44:03.077
I hope so.

44:03.293 --> 44:05.003
Jay says you're pretty determined.

44:05.211 --> 44:07.591
He's been waiting outside
the front of the building...

44:07.797 --> 44:09.927
...with some 40-pound gizmo
for over a month.

44:10.133 --> 44:13.513
- He said you're smart.
- Well, I like to think so.

44:13.720 --> 44:16.720
- And you want to learn this business?
- Yes, sir, I wanna learn.

44:16.973 --> 44:18.933
Have you already started learning
on your own?

44:19.142 --> 44:20.812
Absolutely.

44:21.561 --> 44:23.361
- Jay?
- Yes, sir.

44:23.563 --> 44:25.653
How many times
have you seen Chris?

44:25.899 --> 44:28.529
I don't know.
One too many, apparently.

44:29.152 --> 44:31.492
- Was he ever dressed like this?
- No.

44:31.738 --> 44:33.908
No. Jacket and tie.

44:35.825 --> 44:38.695
First in your class in school?

44:38.954 --> 44:40.754
- High school?
- Yes, sir.

44:41.164 --> 44:44.174
- How many in the class?
- Twelve.

44:44.417 --> 44:46.127
It was a small town.

44:46.586 --> 44:49.916
- I'll say.
- But I was also first in my radar class...

44:50.173 --> 44:53.393
...in the Navy,
and that was a class of 20.

44:55.887 --> 44:57.677
Can I say something?

44:58.848 --> 45:00.558
I'm the type of person...

45:00.767 --> 45:04.017
...if you ask me a question,
and I don't know the answer...

45:04.229 --> 45:06.479
...I'm gonna tell you
that I don't know.

45:06.690 --> 45:08.020
But I bet you what.

45:08.275 --> 45:13.235
I know how to find the answer,
and I will find the answer.

45:14.447 --> 45:16.157
Is that fair enough?

45:17.450 --> 45:18.620
Chris.

45:19.953 --> 45:23.673
What would you say
if a guy walked in for an interview...

45:23.873 --> 45:25.883
...without a shirt on...

45:26.126 --> 45:28.996
...and I hired him?
What would you say?

45:33.300 --> 45:36.340
He must've had on
some really nice pants.

45:51.067 --> 45:54.607
Chris, I don't know how you did it
dressed as a garbage man...

45:54.821 --> 45:57.071
...but you pulled it off.
- Thank you, Mr. Twistle.

45:57.324 --> 45:59.704
Hey, now you can call me Jay.
We'll talk to you soon.

46:00.327 --> 46:02.827
All right, so I'll let you know, Jay.

46:03.663 --> 46:05.923
"You'll let me know, Jay"?
What do you mean?

46:06.166 --> 46:08.076
Yeah, I'll give you a call
tomorrow sometime...

46:08.335 --> 46:10.415
What are you talking...?
You hounded me for this.

46:10.670 --> 46:13.380
- You stood here...
- Listen, there's no salary.

46:13.590 --> 46:14.970
- No.
- I was not aware of that.

46:15.175 --> 46:16.755
My circumstances
have changed some...

46:17.344 --> 46:21.014
...and I need to be certain that I'll be...
- All right. Okay.

46:24.184 --> 46:25.734
Tonight.

46:25.936 --> 46:29.436
I swear I will fill your spot. I promise.

46:29.689 --> 46:32.649
If you back out, you know what
I'll look like to the partners?

46:32.859 --> 46:35.819
Yes, an ass... A-hole.

46:36.112 --> 46:39.532
Yeah, an ass A-hole, all the way.

46:42.452 --> 46:45.002
You are a piece of work.

46:46.039 --> 46:47.579
Tonight.

46:55.882 --> 46:57.842
<i>There was no salary.</i>

46:58.051 --> 47:01.221
<i>Not even a reasonable promise</i>
<i>of a job.</i>

47:07.894 --> 47:12.524
<i>One intern was hired at the end</i>
<i>of the programme from a pool of 20.</i>

47:12.899 --> 47:14.149
<i>And if you weren't that guy...</i>

47:14.401 --> 47:16.741
<i>... you couldn't even apply</i>
<i>the six months' training...</i>

47:16.987 --> 47:18.777
<i>... to another brokerage.</i>

47:21.324 --> 47:23.454
<i>The only resource I would have</i>
<i>for six months...</i>

47:23.660 --> 47:27.580
<i>... would be my six scanners,</i>
<i>which I could still try to sell.</i>

47:28.832 --> 47:32.252
<i>If I sold them all,</i>
<i>maybe we might get by.</i>

48:19.132 --> 48:22.342
- I got him. I got him.
- He's asleep.

48:22.552 --> 48:24.102
All right.

48:30.477 --> 48:32.347
Okay, baby.

48:44.908 --> 48:46.698
