this ball all day and night.

54:30.754 --> 54:32.214
- All right?
- All right.

54:32.422 --> 54:34.262
Okay.

54:35.425 --> 54:37.045
All right, go ahead.

55:00.867 --> 55:02.487
Hey.

55:05.705 --> 55:07.995
Don't ever let somebody tell you...

55:08.208 --> 55:10.748
...you can't do something.

55:11.461 --> 55:13.591
Not even me.

55:14.965 --> 55:18.085
- All right?
- All right.

55:18.802 --> 55:20.972
You got a dream...

55:21.221 --> 55:23.431
...you gotta protect it.

55:24.558 --> 55:26.178
People can't do something
themselves...

55:26.393 --> 55:28.813
...they wanna tell you
you can't do it.

55:33.149 --> 55:36.949
If you want something,
go get it. Period.

55:44.995 --> 55:46.575
Let's go.

55:49.666 --> 55:52.206
Dad, why did we move to a motel?

55:52.419 --> 55:54.879
I told you. Because I'm getting
a better job.

55:56.172 --> 55:59.182
- You gotta trust me, all right?
- I trust you.

55:59.426 --> 56:02.136
All right, here.
Come on, come on. Keep up.

56:03.346 --> 56:06.306
Dad, when's Mom coming back?

56:06.850 --> 56:09.060
Dad, when's Mom coming back?

56:09.269 --> 56:11.479
I don't know, Christopher.

56:11.855 --> 56:13.765
Dad, listen to this.

56:14.024 --> 56:17.444
One day, a man was <i>drownding</i>
in the water.

56:17.694 --> 56:20.114
And a boat came by and said,
"Do you need any help?"

56:20.363 --> 56:22.663
He said, " No, thank you.
God will save me."

56:22.866 --> 56:26.036
Then another boat came by.
Said, "Do you need any help?"

56:26.286 --> 56:28.616
And he said, " No, thank you.
God will save me."

56:28.872 --> 56:30.962
Then he drowned,
and he went to heaven.

56:31.207 --> 56:34.377
And he said, " God,
why didn't you save me?"

56:34.628 --> 56:38.088
And God said, " I sent you
two big boats, you dummy."

56:39.382 --> 56:40.842
Do you like it?

56:41.051 --> 56:43.761
Yeah, that's very funny, man.
Give me your hand.

56:49.809 --> 56:51.439
- Thank you very much, sir.
- Yes, sir.

56:51.645 --> 56:53.265
- You got the bill of sale here.
- Yes.

56:53.480 --> 56:54.860
All the information you'll need.

56:55.065 --> 56:56.685
Thank you very much
for your business.

56:56.900 --> 56:58.400
Thank you.

57:01.154 --> 57:03.874
One hundred, 200,
20, 40, 45, 46...

57:04.074 --> 57:05.704
...7, 8, 9, 10.

57:06.326 --> 57:07.366
Thank you.

57:09.746 --> 57:12.666
- Hey, you want one of those?
- No, it's okay.

57:12.916 --> 57:15.166
Come on, you can have one.
Which one?

57:16.086 --> 57:19.586
- You like that one? How much?
- Twenty-five cents.

57:33.853 --> 57:37.523
<i>This part of my life</i>
<i>is called "Internship."</i>

57:37.774 --> 57:41.074
The 1200 building is
Medley Industrial and Sanko Oil.

57:41.278 --> 57:43.568
The building across the street
is Lee-Ray Shipping.

57:43.780 --> 57:45.660
In a couple weeks,
you'll get call sheets...

57:45.865 --> 57:47.695
...with the phone numbers
of employees...

57:47.951 --> 57:51.041
...from every <i>Fortune 500</i> company
in the financial district.

57:51.371 --> 57:54.041
You will be pooling
from 60 <i>Fortune</i> companies.

57:54.291 --> 57:57.001
You will mainly be cold-calling
potential clients.

57:57.210 --> 58:00.210
But if you have to have lunch
with them, have breakfast with them...

58:00.463 --> 58:03.683
...even baby-sit for them, do whatever
it takes to familiarize them...

58:03.884 --> 58:06.804
...with our packages. We need you
to match their needs and goals...

58:07.053 --> 58:11.933
...to one of our many financial plans.
In essence, you reel them in...

58:12.142 --> 58:14.272
...we'll cook the fish.

58:15.061 --> 58:17.111
Some of you are here
because you know somebody.

58:17.314 --> 58:19.694
Some of you are here because
you think you're somebody.

58:19.983 --> 58:22.443
There's one guy in here
who's gonna be somebody.

58:22.652 --> 58:24.862
That person's gonna be the guy...

58:25.071 --> 58:27.321
...who can turn this into this.

58:27.574 --> 58:30.624
Eight hundred thousand
in commission dollars.

58:31.161 --> 58:32.951
You, you, help me hand these out.

58:33.830 --> 58:36.880
This is going to be your bible.

58:37.083 --> 58:38.423
You'll eat with it.

58:38.668 --> 58:40.298
- You'll drink with it.
- <i>It was simple.</i>

58:40.503 --> 58:43.473
<i>X number of calls</i>
<i>equals X number of prospects.</i>

58:43.673 --> 58:46.643
<i>X number of prospects</i>
<i>equals X number of customers.</i>

58:46.927 --> 58:50.007
<i>X number of customers</i>
<i>equals X number of dollars...</i>

58:50.263 --> 58:52.393
- <i>... in the company's pocket.</i>
- Your board exam.

58:52.599 --> 58:58.479
Last year, we had an intern score
a 96.4 percent on the written exam.

58:58.688 --> 59:02.028
He wasn't chosen.
It's not a simple pass-fail.

59:02.275 --> 59:05.645
It's an evaluation tool we use
to separate applicants.

59:05.862 --> 59:08.202
Be safe, score a hundred.

59:09.199 --> 59:12.329
Okay, let's take a break.
Be back in 10.

59:21.628 --> 59:24.548
- Hey, Mr. Frohm. Chris.
- Hi.

59:24.798 --> 59:26.968
