1:08:39.102 --> 1:08:41.152
We don't have a car anymore.

1:08:41.354 --> 1:08:43.574
Yep, I know.

1:08:47.110 --> 1:08:50.160
I'm gonna need to take you
with me this weekend.

1:08:50.363 --> 1:08:52.623
A couple of doctors' offices.

1:08:53.116 --> 1:08:56.906
- On sales calls, okay?
- Okay.

1:08:59.873 --> 1:09:03.843
Then, possibly,
we'll go to the football game.

1:09:04.044 --> 1:09:06.884
- Really?
- Possibly.

1:09:07.297 --> 1:09:09.757
- All right?
- All right.

1:09:09.966 --> 1:09:12.046
Come on, finish up.

1:09:12.552 --> 1:09:15.512
- Are you sure?
- Possibly.

1:09:16.723 --> 1:09:18.313
Really?

1:09:48.255 --> 1:09:52.795
- Are you bringing it to the game?
- Yeah, I don't wanna leave it.

1:09:53.009 --> 1:09:55.969
And maybe
we're going to the game.

1:09:57.514 --> 1:10:01.434
- Where are we going now?
- To see someone about my job.

1:10:01.851 --> 1:10:03.481
I don't understand.

1:10:03.687 --> 1:10:06.897
- You don't understand what?
- Are we going to the game?

1:10:07.107 --> 1:10:09.647
I said possibly
we're going to the game.

1:10:09.859 --> 1:10:12.199
- You know what "possibly" means?
- Like probably.

1:10:12.445 --> 1:10:15.025
No, "probably" means there's
a good chance that we're going.

1:10:15.282 --> 1:10:17.992
"Possibly" means we might,
we might not.

1:10:18.201 --> 1:10:21.251
- What does "probably" mean?
- It means we have a good chance.

1:10:21.454 --> 1:10:22.834
And what does "possibly" mean?

1:10:23.039 --> 1:10:25.499
- I know what it means.
- What does it mean?

1:10:25.709 --> 1:10:28.249
It means that we're not going
to the game.

1:10:29.963 --> 1:10:33.173
- How did you get so smart?
- Because you're smart.

1:10:38.305 --> 1:10:41.015
- Are we there?
- Yeah.

1:10:46.563 --> 1:10:48.113
- Mr. Ribbon.
- Yes?

1:10:48.315 --> 1:10:51.185
How are you, sir?
Chris Gardner. Dean Witter.

1:10:51.735 --> 1:10:54.195
- Oh, hi. Hi.
- This is my son, Christopher.

1:10:54.404 --> 1:10:55.914
- Hi.
- Hey, Christopher.

1:10:56.156 --> 1:10:58.526
- What are you doing up here?
- I came to apologise...

1:10:58.742 --> 1:11:01.372
...for missing our appointment.
- You didn't need to come up.

1:11:01.578 --> 1:11:04.208
We were in the neighbourhood
visiting a very close friend...

1:11:04.414 --> 1:11:07.924
...and I wanted to take this opportunity
to say thank you for your time.

1:11:08.168 --> 1:11:10.958
- I know you probably waited for me.
- Little bit.

1:11:11.171 --> 1:11:13.721
I want you to know
that I do not take that for granted.

1:11:13.924 --> 1:11:15.974
Oh, come on. What's that?

1:11:16.218 --> 1:11:19.638
Oh, it's an Osteo National
bone-density scanner.

1:11:20.472 --> 1:11:23.392
A company I bought into
prior to going to work at Witter.

1:11:23.600 --> 1:11:26.230
- I have a meeting after the game.
- You're going to the game?

1:11:26.436 --> 1:11:28.226
- Yeah.
- Possibly.

1:11:29.272 --> 1:11:30.612
- Possibly.
- We're going too.

1:11:30.857 --> 1:11:32.477
I'm taking my son, Tim.
My 12-year-old.

1:11:32.692 --> 1:11:33.822
We were just leaving. Tim!

1:11:34.110 --> 1:11:36.030
Listen, we'll get out of your way.

1:11:36.279 --> 1:11:38.949
Again, thank you very much,
and I'm sorry about the other day.

1:11:39.199 --> 1:11:41.239
And I hope that
we can reschedule for later.

1:11:41.451 --> 1:11:42.951
- You got it.
- Thank you very much.

1:11:43.203 --> 1:11:44.833
You take care. Here, come on.

1:11:45.038 --> 1:11:46.368
- Say bye-bye, Chris.
- Bye.

1:11:46.623 --> 1:11:48.213
Bye, Christopher.

1:11:48.458 --> 1:11:49.918
Hey, you guys wanna
come with us?

1:11:50.126 --> 1:11:53.086
- What...? To Candlestick?
- We're going now. Come with us.

1:11:53.296 --> 1:11:56.416
- Where are your seats?
- We've... We're upper deck.

1:11:56.633 --> 1:11:57.883
We got a box. Come on.

1:11:58.134 --> 1:12:00.264
- You wanna sit in the box?
- No.

1:12:01.471 --> 1:12:05.391
It's not actually a box.
It's, you know, a private section.

1:12:05.642 --> 1:12:08.062
It's more comfortable.
You wanna go?

1:12:08.728 --> 1:12:12.438
- Okay.
- Okay, kids in the back.

1:12:13.066 --> 1:12:15.276
Hey, why don't you just put that
in your car?

1:12:17.988 --> 1:12:20.948
- Yeah, okay. Sure, sure.
- We don't have a car.

1:12:21.825 --> 1:12:24.035
- Oh, my...
- What happened?

1:12:24.244 --> 1:12:25.624
I think I got stung by a bee.

1:12:25.829 --> 1:12:28.749
- You all right?
- Oh, yeah. Goodness. I'm fine.

1:12:28.999 --> 1:12:31.539
- You're not allergic or anything?
- No, no, no.

1:12:31.793 --> 1:12:35.093
- Where'd he get you?
- Just right at the back of my head.

1:12:35.338 --> 1:12:37.718
- Are you okay?
- Yeah, I'm fine, Christopher.

1:12:37.924 --> 1:12:40.054
- Does it hurt?
- Christopher, I'm fine.

1:12:40.260 --> 1:12:44.140
- Let me see.
- Christopher, sit back. Sit back.

1:12:44.347 --> 1:12:46.677
<i>Thomas Jefferson mentions</i>
<i>happiness a couple times...</i>

1:12:46.933 --> 1:12:49.693
<i>... in the Declaration</i>
<i>of Independence.</i>

1:12:50.145 --> 1:12:52.685
<i>May seem like a strange word</i>
<i>to be in that document...</i>

1:12:52.939 --> 1:12:57.819
<i>... but he was sort of...</i>
<i>He was an artist.</i>

1:12:58.111 --> 1:13:02.661
<i>He called the English</i>
<i>"the disturbers of our harmony."</i>

1:13:02.949 --> 1:13:04.699
<i>And I remember standing there</i>
<i>that day...</i>

1:13:04.951 --> 1:13:07.201
<i>... thinking about</i>
<i>the disturbers of mine.</i>

1:13:07.454 --> 1:13:11.674
<i>Questions I had.</i>
<i>Whether all this was good.</i>

1:13:12.042 --> 1:13:13.842
<i>Whether I'd make it.</i>

1:13:16.880 --> 1:13:19.840
<i>And Walter Ribbon</i>
<i>and his Pacific Bell pension money...</i>

1:13:20.050 --> 1:13:21.380
<i>... which was millions.</i>

1:13:21.635 --> 1:13:23.215
Yeah!

1:13:23.720 --> 1:13:26.600
<i>It was a way to another place.</i>

1:13:27.390 --> 1:13:29.480
Wow, this is...

1:13:29.893 --> 1:13:31.813
This is the way
to watch a football game here.

1:13:32.062 --> 1:13:35.112
- Thank you very much for this, really.
- Hey, it's my pleasure, Chris.

1:13:35.315 --> 1:13:38.565
And, Mr. Ribbon, I also wanna thank
you for giving me the opportunity...

1:13:38.818 --> 1:13:41.658
...to discuss the asset management
capabilities of Dean Witter...

1:13:41.988 --> 1:13:44.118
...which we believe
to be far superior...

1:13:44.324 --> 1:13:46.914
...to anything you got going
over at Morgan Stanley.

1:13:47.160 --> 1:13:48.950
Really, I think you're gonna
be blown away.

1:13:49.496 --> 1:13:54.206
Point blank, Dean Witter needs to be
managing your retirement portfolio.

1:13:54.417 --> 1:13:56.957
You know, I didn't have any notion
that you were new there.

1:13:57.170 --> 1:14:00.630
I like you, but there's not a chance
I'm gonna let you direct our fund.

1:14:00.840 --> 1:14:02.930
That's just not gonna happen
anytime soon, buddy.

1:14:03.134 --> 1:14:06.264
So, you know, come on, relax.
Enjoy the game. Go, go, go!

1:14:07.264 --> 1:14:08.524
Yes!

1:14:11.518 --> 1:14:13.558
Yes! Yeah!

1:14:18.275 --> 1:14:19.315
- Here you go.
- All right.

1:14:19.526 --> 1:14:21.276
I've had a few ideas
already, absolutely.

1:14:21.528 --> 1:14:24.068
- Chris, I'll talk to you later.
- I'm gonna give you a call.

1:14:24.281 --> 1:14:25.951
Nice to meet you, Chris.
Give me a call.

1:14:26.199 --> 1:14:27.739
Yes, absolutely. Thank you.

1:14:34.624 --> 1:14:37.344
- Bye.
- Bye, Christopher.

1:15:06.823 --> 1:15:11.373
<i>After four months, we had sold</i>
<i>all our scanners.</i>

1:15:12.662 --> 1:15:14.042
<i>It seemed we were making it.</i>

1:15:14.998 --> 1:15:16.208
What's the...

1:15:16.583 --> 1:15:19.093
...fastest animal in the world?
- Jackrabbit.

1:15:21.296 --> 1:15:24.716
<i>It seemed we were doing good.</i>

1:15:24.925 --> 1:15:26.675
<i>Until one day...</i>

1:15:26.968 --> 1:15:28.638
<i>... that day...</i>

1:15:29.179 --> 1:15:31.139
<i>... that letter brought me</i>
<i>back to earth.</i>

1:15:38.521 --> 1:15:41.111
<i>This part of my life is called</i>
<i>"Paying Taxes."</i>

1:15:43.193 --> 1:15:44.493
<i>If you didn't pay them...</i>

1:15:44.736 --> 1:15:47.606
<i>... the government could stick</i>
<i>their hands into your bank account...</i>

1:15:48.281 --> 1:15:49.451
<i>... and take your money.</i>

1:15:49.699 --> 1:15:50.659
Dad.

1:15:50.867 --> 1:15:52.867
<i>No warning. Nothing.</i>

1:15:53.078 --> 1:15:56.208
It can't be too late.
That's my money.

1:15:56.456 --> 1:15:59.536
How is somebody just gonna
just take my money?

1:15:59.876 --> 1:16:01.166
I was... I was...

1:16:01.419 --> 1:16:04.669
Listen, I...
That's all the money that I have.

1:16:04.881 --> 1:16:09.181
You cannot go into my bank acc...
No...

1:16:09.386 --> 1:16:11.756
<i>It was the 25th of September.</i>

1:16:11.972 --> 1:16:13.682
<i>I remember that day.</i>

1:16:13.932 --> 1:16:15.982
<i>Because that's the day</i>
<i>that I found out...</i>

1:16:16.226 --> 1:16:21.306
<i>... there was only 21 dollars</i>
<i>and 33 cents left in my bank account.</i>

1:16:21.565 --> 1:16:23.185
<i>I was broke.</i>

1:16:33.577 --> 1:16:35.867
- Dressed yet?
- No.

1:16:39.749 --> 1:16:43.089
Chris! Chris!
Don't jerk me around, okay, Chris?

1:16:43.336 --> 1:16:46.046
I'm not jerking you around, Ralph,
all right? I'm gonna get it.

1:16:46.256 --> 1:16:49.836
- I need that money now, not later.
- When I get it, you get it, Ralph.

1:16:50.093 --> 1:16:51.933
Now!

1:16:55.640 --> 1:16:57.680
Hey, what's happening, man?

1:16:57.934 --> 1:17:00.774
Wayne, I need to get
that $14 from you.

1:17:02.439 --> 1:17:04.319
I thought I didn't owe you that now.

1:17:04.524 --> 1:17:07.574
- What? Why?
- Why what?

1:17:07.777 --> 1:17:10.157
Why would you think
you don't owe me my money?

1:17:10.363 --> 1:17:12.323
I helped you move.

1:17:14.618 --> 1:17:17.448
You drove me two blocks, Wayne.

1:17:17.704 --> 1:17:19.414
That's 200 yards.

1:17:19.623 --> 1:17:21.583
It's been four months, Wayne.

1:17:21.791 --> 1:17:25.381
I need my money. I need my money.
I need my money right now.

1:17:25.629 --> 1:17:27.919
- I don't have it, man. I'm sorry.
- Go get my money.

1:17:28.131 --> 1:17:30.341
- Wayne, get my mo...
- I really don't, man. It's $14.

1:17:30.592 --> 1:17:32.262
It's my $14!
Go get my money!

1:17:32.469 --> 1:17:35.009
- All of this for $14.
- Get my money, Wayne.

1:17:53.406 --> 1:17:55.526
Dad, look at me!

1:17:55.992 --> 1:17:57.702
Dad.

1:17:58.745 --> 1:18:02.245
- Should I go?
- Sure, man. Why not?

1:18:18.348 --> 1:18:19.348
- Stay here.
- Dad, look.

1:18:19.599 --> 1:18:21.139
- No, no. Stay right here.
- Dad.

1:18:21.351 --> 1:18:24.151
Did you hear what I said?
Did you hear me?

1:18:29.276 --> 1:18:32.736
- Dad, where you going?
- Hey, what did I say?

1:18:35.782 --> 1:18:37.412
Dad!

1:18:37.617 --> 1:18:40.997
Dad, wait! Dad!

1:18:49.212 --> 1:18:51.212
- Dad.
- I gotta...

1:18:51.423 --> 1:18:54.803
I gotta get back to the '60s, man.
That's what I wanna do.

1:18:55.051 --> 1:18:59.311
When I was younger. I wanna see
Jimi Hendrix do that guitar on fire.

1:19:02.392 --> 1:19:05.062
Bring back my time machine!

1:19:06.396 --> 1:19:08.056
Bring my time machine back!

1:19:16.948 --> 1:19:20.538
- Dad, where are we going?
- Be quiet.

1:19:21.161 --> 1:19:23.871
Go get your things. Go.

1:19:47.145 --> 1:19:48.765
- Chris?
- Yes.

1:19:49.022 --> 1:19:52.902
Dr. Telm can't get back to meet you.
I'm sorry.

1:20:04.120 --> 1:20:06.540
Where are we going now?

1:20:07.290 --> 1:20:10.590
We gotta... We gotta
see somebody else.

1:20:12.712 --> 1:20:14.802
I'm tired.

1:20:16.841 --> 1:20:18.431
I know.

1:20:25.809 --> 1:20:29.939
Doesn't seem to be functioning
right now.

1:20:30.397 --> 1:20:32.647
- I have to go now, Chris.
- No, no, no.

1:20:32.899 --> 1:20:36.739
Just give me a second. I'm sure
I'm gonna be able to figure it out.

1:20:38.572 --> 1:20:40.822
Chris. Chris, just come back
when it's working.

1:20:41.074 --> 1:20:43.874
- No, no. I have to fix it now.
- No.

1:20:44.077 --> 1:20:49.287
Look, I'll still be putting money
in the office, then, all right?

1:20:49.499 --> 1:20:51.629
I really have to go, Chris.

1:20:52.878 --> 1:20:54.548
Thank you. Thank you.

1:20:54.754 --> 1:20:56.634
Thank you for your time.
I appreciate it.

1:20:56.840 --> 1:20:58.510
I'll see you soon.

1:21:50.560 --> 1:21:52.940
Why are our things here?

1:21:53.980 --> 1:21:55.570
Dad.

1:22:38.149 --> 1:22:40.819
- Let's go. Come on.
- Where?

1:22:42.445 --> 1:22:44.735
- Just out of here.
- Why?

1:22:44.948 --> 1:22:47.948
- We can't stay here tonight.
- Yes, we can. Open the door!

1:22:48.201 --> 1:22:51.121
- Did you hear what I said? Let's go.
- Open the door!

1:22:52.831 --> 1:22:56.711
Hey, did you hear what I said?
Stop it.

1:22:56.960 --> 1:22:58.420
Stop it.

1:23:02.674 --> 1:23:04.094
Come on.

1:23:13.226 --> 1:23:14.686
Come on.

1:23:31.661 --> 1:23:33.331
<i>Wayne!</i>

1:23:34.456 --> 1:23:36.286
Wayne!

1:23:43.506 --> 1:23:45.796
Wayne!

1:24:01.358 --> 1:24:05.068
Get up. Stand up. Come on.

1:24:20.919 --> 1:24:22.959
Where are we going?

1:24:25.131 --> 1:24:28.471
- Dad, where are we going?
- I don't know.

1:24:43.984 --> 1:24:46.364
It's not a time machine.

1:24:46.570 --> 1:24:47.990
Dad.

1:24:48.405 --> 1:24:49.695
It's not a time machine.

1:24:49.906 --> 1:24:53.156
The guy said it was a time machine.
It's not a time machine. He was wrong.

1:24:53.577 --> 1:24:55.907
- What guy?
- The guy. He was at the park.

1:24:56.162 --> 1:24:58.042
He said it was a time machine.

1:25:04.421 --> 1:25:05.631
Yes, it is.

1:25:07.257 --> 1:25:09.007
No, it's not.

1:25:11.011 --> 1:25:12.971
- It is.
- No, it's not.

1:25:19.227 --> 1:25:23.727
All we gotta do is push
this black button right here.

1:25:26.943 --> 1:25:28.073
Wanna push it?

1:25:32.616 --> 1:25:34.236
Okay.

1:25:35.785 --> 1:25:37.365
Come on.

1:25:38.872 --> 1:25:40.502
Come on, man.

1:25:46.213 --> 1:25:47.263
Right here.

1:25:47.631 --> 1:25:49.261
Wait a minute.
Where you wanna go?

1:25:49.633 --> 1:25:51.593
I don't know.
Some place from before.

1:25:52.135 --> 1:25:53.385
You gotta close your eyes.

1:25:53.678 --> 1:25:55.558
You close your eyes. I wanna see.

1:25:57.724 --> 1:26:00.144
All right, come on.
We'll push it together.

1:26:05.982 --> 1:26:07.782
You gotta close your eyes.
Close your eyes.

1:26:08.485 --> 1:26:10.645
It takes a few seconds.

1:26:13.073 --> 1:26:14.953
Oh, my goodness.

1:26:15.158 --> 1:26:17.368
Open, open, open!

1:26:20.789 --> 1:26:23.419
- What is it?
- Dinosaurs.

1:26:23.667 --> 1:26:25.787
- Where?
- You don't see all these dinosaurs?

1:26:27.170 --> 1:26:30.840
Look around.
Look at all these dinosaurs.

1:26:32.592 --> 1:26:34.972
- Do you see them?
- Yeah.

1:26:35.178 --> 1:26:36.598
Wait. Come on, come on.

1:26:36.846 --> 1:26:38.136
- Wait, watch out.
- What is it?

1:26:38.348 --> 1:26:40.388
Don't step in the fire.
We're cavemen.

1:26:40.767 --> 1:26:42.977
We need this fire,
because there's no electricity...

1:26:43.228 --> 1:26:44.598
...and it's cold out here, okay?

1:26:45.313 --> 1:26:47.653
- Watch out!
- Whoa! Oh, my good... A <i>T. rex.</i>

1:26:47.899 --> 1:26:51.489
Get your stuff.
Get your stuff. Get it.

1:26:52.529 --> 1:26:55.569
- We gotta find someplace safe.
- Like what?

1:26:55.782 --> 1:26:57.742
We need a cave.

1:26:57.951 --> 1:26:59.041
A cave?

1:26:59.286 --> 1:27:01.286
- We gotta find a cave. Come on.
- Okay.

1:27:01.496 --> 1:27:03.246
Come on, come on.

1:27:04.875 --> 1:27:06.205
Watch your back! Look out.

1:27:06.459 --> 1:27:08.459
Here it is. Here's a cave. Come on.

1:27:08.712 --> 1:27:11.552
Right here, right here.
Go, go, go.

1:27:11.798 --> 1:27:13.008
Go ahead. Get in.

1:27:13.216 --> 1:27:15.046
Hurry, hurry, hurry.

1:27:18.680 --> 1:27:22.430
- Are we safe?
- Yeah, I think so.

1:28:30.460 --> 1:28:32.050
Hey.

1:28:33.630 --> 1:28:35.260
- How you doing, Jay?
- I'm doing good.

1:28:35.465 --> 1:28:36.925
How are you getting along?

1:28:37.133 --> 1:28:39.303
- Good. I'm good.
- You doing good?

1:28:39.511 --> 1:28:42.061
- How you doing?
- I'm doing great.

1:28:43.181 --> 1:28:44.811
Where you going?

1:28:48.144 --> 1:28:51.114
I... Sacramento.

1:28:51.815 --> 1:28:54.435
Because I'm trying to move
a couple guys from...

1:28:54.651 --> 1:28:57.281
They're at PacBell,
and I'm trying to bring them over...

1:28:57.487 --> 1:28:58.737
Get them over to us.

1:28:58.989 --> 1:29:00.659
So they got me
going out there golfing.

1:29:00.866 --> 1:29:02.696
Awesome.

1:29:02.951 --> 1:29:04.871
Hey, let them win a round.

1:29:10.083 --> 1:29:12.043
Deborah, someone's asking for you.

1:29:12.294 --> 1:29:15.344
- Where?
- He's outside. Please come with me.

1:29:23.221 --> 1:29:26.681
- Hi.
- How you doing?

1:29:28.101 --> 1:29:30.651
- Can I ask you a question?
- Sure.

1:29:32.856 --> 1:29:34.476
We need a room.

1:29:35.108 --> 1:29:38.068
Just until I can fix this and sell it.

1:29:38.278 --> 1:29:40.908
- There's just some glass work.
- Let me stop you right there.

1:29:41.114 --> 1:29:43.584
- I wish I could help you...
- This is my son, Christopher.

1:29:43.950 --> 1:29:45.910
- He's 5 years old.
- Hi, baby.

1:29:46.161 --> 1:29:49.161
- We need some place to stay.
- Okay, and I would love to help you...

1:29:49.372 --> 1:29:52.252
...but we don't take men here.
It's only women and children.

1:29:52.459 --> 1:29:55.499
He can stay here, but you have
to find someplace else to go.

1:29:55.712 --> 1:29:57.132
We gotta stay together.

1:29:57.380 --> 1:29:58.670
We got... We're...

1:29:58.882 --> 1:30:00.722
- Okay, listen.
- You gotta have some place...

1:30:00.967 --> 1:30:03.797
Try Glide Memorial.
The building books up at 5.

1:30:04.054 --> 1:30:05.514
So you hurry up. There's a line.

1:30:05.722 --> 1:30:09.102
- And where is it? Come on.
- Ellis and Jones.

1:30:44.344 --> 1:30:49.984
Hey, everybody. We have
four spots left, and that's all.

1:30:50.392 --> 1:30:53.272
- Man.
- Hey, come on, man.

1:30:53.478 --> 1:30:54.688
- Come on.
- Come on, what?

1:30:54.938 --> 1:30:56.478
- Hey, that's my spot.
- Back off.

1:30:56.690 --> 1:30:59.110
Come on, don't do this to me.
Don't...

1:31:01.528 --> 1:31:03.068
Dad!

1:31:03.530 --> 1:31:05.570
Stop it! Break it up!
Break it up!

1:31:05.782 --> 1:31:07.372
Stop! Stop!

1:31:07.576 --> 1:31:09.866
Get out of line, both of you.
Both of you.

1:31:10.120 --> 1:31:12.660
I was here first. They told me
that we had to be on time.

1:31:12.956 --> 1:31:14.916
I got here on time. I was in line.

1:31:15.125 --> 1:31:16.875
I came from work, I got my son.

1:31:17.127 --> 1:31:19.587
I was here on time.
We were here on time!

1:31:19.796 --> 1:31:21.416
He sliced in front of him in line.

1:31:21.631 --> 1:31:23.931
- Who did?
- He did.

1:31:24.217 --> 1:31:28.717
Come on, come on, Rodney.
Come on. Let's go. Get out of line.

1:31:37.981 --> 1:31:39.941
That's it. No more.

1:31:46.990 --> 1:31:49.950
- What's your favourite colour?
- Green.

1:31:50.160 --> 1:31:51.410
Green?

1:31:51.661 --> 1:31:54.621
- What do you like that's green?
- Trees.

1:31:54.831 --> 1:31:57.791
Trees. What else?

1:31:58.001 --> 1:31:59.461
Holly.

1:32:01.254 --> 1:32:05.224
- Holly. What's holly?
- The Christmas stuff.

1:32:06.009 --> 1:32:07.969
Christmas stuff.

1:32:08.762 --> 1:32:10.512
What's that?

1:32:13.767 --> 1:32:16.647
I guess they want us to go to sleep.

1:32:23.193 --> 1:32:28.203
Here you go. We gotta make sure
Captain America's warm in there.

1:32:28.698 --> 1:32:30.368
Can he breathe?

1:32:30.617 --> 1:32:32.827
- He's good?
- Yeah.

1:32:33.286 --> 1:32:35.286
- I gotta go work on the scanner...
- Don't go.

1:32:35.539 --> 1:32:38.669
No, no, no. I'm gonna be
right outside the door.

1:32:38.875 --> 1:32:42.995
All right? I'm just gonna be right there.
I'll leave the door open a little bit.

1:32:43.547 --> 1:32:46.217
And I'll be able to hear you
if you call me.

1:32:46.383 --> 1:32:48.893
I wanna go home.

1:32:50.971 --> 1:32:54.771
But that's why I gotta
work on the scanner.

1:32:55.725 --> 1:32:57.475
All right?

1:32:57.727 --> 1:32:59.597
I'm gonna go out there.

1:32:59.813 --> 1:33:03.193
I'm gonna leave the door open.
I'll be right up the stairs.

1:33:04.317 --> 1:33:05.987
I'll be able to hear you
if you call me.

1:33:06.987 --> 1:33:09.067
- All right?
- All right.

1:33:09.322 --> 1:33:11.622
You gotta trust me, okay?

1:33:11.825 --> 1:33:13.865
You gotta trust me.

1:33:14.744 --> 1:33:17.374
I trust you. I trust you.

1:33:17.581 --> 1:33:19.041
I trust you.

1:33:19.249 --> 1:33:22.209
- I can't hear you.
- I trust you. I trust you.

1:33:26.089 --> 1:33:27.759
Give me a kiss.

1:33:40.437 --> 1:33:43.397
- I'll just be a little while, okay?
- All right.

1:33:43.857 --> 1:33:46.317
- I'll be right here.
- Okay.

1:33:46.526 --> 1:33:48.736
- Can you still hear me?
- Yeah.

1:33:48.945 --> 1:33:50.405
- Can you hear me?
- Yeah.

1:33:50.697 --> 1:33:53.117
- Do you trust me?
- Yeah.

1:34:40.330 --> 1:34:42.000
- Yeah.
- Like that?

1:34:42.249 --> 1:34:45.879
- Yeah, put that...
- Then you go like that.

1:34:46.086 --> 1:34:49.586
- Is that okay?
- I don't know. What do you think?

1:34:49.839 --> 1:34:50.839
Good.

1:34:52.175 --> 1:34:54.425
Let's go. Get your stuff.

1:34:55.679 --> 1:34:58.639
- Dad, why don't you leave it?
- We can't.

1:34:58.848 --> 1:35:00.978
We're gonna have
a different room later.

1:35:01.184 --> 1:35:02.734
Go.

1:35:08.108 --> 1:35:09.438
Hey, Chris.

1:35:09.693 --> 1:35:12.993
- Hey, good morning, Mr. Frakesh.
- What's up?

1:35:14.030 --> 1:35:15.160
Work trip.

1:35:15.365 --> 1:35:17.655
Your wife, Martha, works at
PacBell also, correct?

1:35:17.868 --> 1:35:19.618
- Yes, she does.
- And you guys are both...

1:35:19.870 --> 1:35:21.500
...looking to retire at the same time?

1:35:21.705 --> 1:35:23.785
We'd like to retire
and maintain our lifestyle...

1:35:24.040 --> 1:35:25.420
...without paying a lot of taxes.

1:35:25.625 --> 1:35:29.125
So basically, you want nobody's hands
in your pockets but your own?

1:35:29.713 --> 1:35:31.633
Are you familiar with
tax-free municipal?

1:35:31.882 --> 1:35:33.722
<i>I learned to finish my work quickly.</i>

1:35:34.050 --> 1:35:36.220
<i>I had to finish quickly.</i>

1:35:36.553 --> 1:35:40.063
<i>To get in line at Glide by 5.</i>

1:35:43.810 --> 1:35:45.690
Come on.

1:35:46.229 --> 1:35:47.769
Come on.

1:35:51.902 --> 1:35:54.652
Hold that bus! Hold the bus!

1:35:55.572 --> 1:35:57.282
My Captain America!

1:35:57.574 --> 1:35:59.834
Dad! Dad! Dad!

1:36:00.076 --> 1:36:03.286
Stop it! Shut up! Shut up!

1:36:05.665 --> 1:36:07.665
- Why don't you let the lady in?
- Hey, back up.

1:36:07.918 --> 1:36:10.918
- Hey, man, that's not cool.
- Back up! Back up!

1:36:19.262 --> 1:36:20.722
Come on.

1:36:23.767 --> 1:36:25.937
Dad, we need to get it!

1:36:28.605 --> 1:36:31.185
<i>The important thing about</i>
<i>that freedom train...</i>

1:36:31.441 --> 1:36:33.571
<i>... is it's got to climb mountains.</i>

1:36:33.777 --> 1:36:36.527
<i>We all have to deal with mountains.</i>

1:36:36.780 --> 1:36:39.660
<i>You know, mountains</i>
<i>that go way up high.</i>

1:36:40.116 --> 1:36:42.076
And mountains that go
deep and low.

1:36:42.285 --> 1:36:43.575
- Amen, preacher!
- Yes.

1:36:43.787 --> 1:36:46.077
We know what those mountains are,
here at Glide.

1:36:46.373 --> 1:36:48.503
We sing about them.

1:36:49.292 --> 1:36:54.802
<i>Lord, don't move that mountain</i>

1:36:56.216 --> 1:37:02.636
<i>Give me strength to climb it</i>

1:37:03.139 --> 1:37:09.809
<i>Please don't move</i>
<i>That stumbling block</i>

1:37:10.063 --> 1:37:16.613
<i>But lead me, Lord, around it</i>

1:37:18.238 --> 1:37:23.288
<i>My burdens, they get so heavy</i>

1:37:25.161 --> 1:37:30.751
<i>Seems hard to bear</i>

1:37:31.668 --> 1:37:35.258
<i>But I won't give up</i>
<i>No, no</i>

1:37:35.505 --> 1:37:37.465
<i>Because you promised me</i>

1:37:37.674 --> 1:37:44.434
<i>You'd meet me at the altar of prayer</i>

1:37:44.681 --> 1:37:52.151
- <i>Lord don't move that mountain</i>
- <i>Please don't move that mountain</i>

1:37:52.355 --> 1:37:57.645
<i>But give me strength to climb it</i>

1:37:59.863 --> 1:38:01.873
When's your test?

1:38:03.116 --> 1:38:04.576
Tomorrow.

1:38:08.955 --> 1:38:10.745
Are you ready?

1:38:14.711 --> 1:38:16.091
Of course.

1:38:55.252 --> 1:38:56.502
Thank you, sir.

1:39:05.929 --> 1:39:08.059
- Hey. How you doing?
- Hey.

1:39:12.102 --> 1:39:15.062
So did you finish the whole thing,
or you have to go somewhere?

1:39:15.272 --> 1:39:17.732
I have to go somewhere.

1:39:18.358 --> 1:39:21.148
- But I finished the whole thing too.
- Oh, good.

1:39:21.361 --> 1:39:23.281
- You?
- Yeah.

1:39:23.780 --> 1:39:26.740
- How'd you feel about the graphs?
- Easy.

1:39:27.784 --> 1:39:31.834
I struggled with the essay question
on the back. What did you write?

1:39:32.038 --> 1:39:35.668
- Essay question?
- Yeah, on the back.

1:39:45.635 --> 1:39:46.925
Hey, Chris.

1:39:47.137 --> 1:39:50.427
- Hey. Jeff, right? 49ers game.
- Yeah.

1:39:50.640 --> 1:39:54.100
- Yeah, you were gonna give me a call?
- I never actually got your number.

1:39:55.896 --> 1:39:57.806
Here's my number.
Call me, okay?

1:39:58.064 --> 1:40:00.734
Yes, sir. Absolutely.
Thank you very much.

1:40:01.484 --> 1:40:05.244
Chris, you got five bucks?
I left my wallet upstairs.

1:40:05.488 --> 1:40:07.698
Let me run up and grab that
for you, Mr. Frohm.

1:40:07.908 --> 1:40:10.908
No, I gotta be at CAL Bank at 4,
and I'm late.

1:40:16.333 --> 1:40:18.463
- I'll pay you back, honest.
- Five is good?

1:40:18.668 --> 1:40:22.298
Five is lovely. Thank you.
Thank you.

1:40:35.685 --> 1:40:38.145
That's it. That's the room quota.

1:40:38.521 --> 1:40:41.271
There's no more space.
You gotta head out.

1:40:41.524 --> 1:40:44.364
That's it for today.
Come back tomorrow.

1:40:44.611 --> 1:40:47.571
All the rooms are full.
It's completely full.

1:40:47.781 --> 1:40:52.081
That's it. Just keep heading out.
Come back tomorrow.

1:41:27.070 --> 1:41:28.820
You like it?

1:42:19.873 --> 1:42:23.543
Twenty. One, two, three, four.

1:42:26.630 --> 1:42:30.260
Now, here's your bulb,
and there's your ferrite core inductor.

1:42:30.467 --> 1:42:33.257
- How much?
- Eight dollars.

1:42:34.387 --> 1:42:37.677
- What's that?
- It's to repair the light.

1:42:37.891 --> 1:42:39.941
Can I see it?

1:42:41.811 --> 1:42:44.901
Yeah, sure. Just don't break it.

1:42:45.148 --> 1:42:49.608
Unless you wanna sleep in a room
with me for the rest of your life.

1:42:50.820 --> 1:42:52.660
I don't mind.

1:42:53.156 --> 1:42:54.946
Yeah, you will.

1:43:11.258 --> 1:43:13.638
Why don't you
get some sleep, okay?

1:43:13.843 --> 1:43:14.973
Okay.

1:43:15.178 --> 1:43:18.308
- Warm enough?
- Yeah.

1:43:18.598 --> 1:43:20.228
All right.

1:43:22.352 --> 1:43:25.232
Did Mom leave because of me?

1:43:28.608 --> 1:43:32.778
- What?
- Did Mom leave because of me?

1:43:37.367 --> 1:43:41.867
Don't... Don't even think
something like that.

1:43:42.956 --> 1:43:45.076
Mom left because of Mom.

1:43:45.292 --> 1:43:47.542
And you didn't have anything
to do with that, okay?

1:43:48.295 --> 1:43:50.165
Okay.

1:44:00.056 --> 1:44:02.056
You're a good papa.

1:44:09.900 --> 1:44:11.900
All right, go to sleep.

1:44:12.736 --> 1:44:15.656
- I love you.
- I love you too.

1:45:12.128 --> 1:45:14.088
So far, so good, Chris.

1:45:20.220 --> 1:45:22.760
- It works.
- Thank you very much.

1:45:22.973 --> 1:45:26.773
<i>Two hundred and fifty dollars.</i>
<i>Four more weeks of oxygen.</i>

1:45:27.143 --> 1:45:31.363
One hundred, 20, 40, 60, 80, 200.

1:45:31.565 --> 1:45:34.315
Twenty, 30, 40, 50.

1:45:35.485 --> 1:45:37.105
- Anything else?
- Nope, that's it.

1:45:37.320 --> 1:45:38.610
Thank you. Thank you.

1:45:38.822 --> 1:45:40.782
- You ready?
- Yep.

1:45:42.742 --> 1:45:45.622
- Are we going to the church place?
- No.

1:45:45.829 --> 1:45:47.789
Where are we going, then?

1:45:48.582 --> 1:45:51.132
- Probably stay at a hotel.
- A hotel?

1:45:51.334 --> 1:45:52.424
Just for the night.

1:45:52.669 --> 1:45:55.379
We can go back to the cave
if you like.

1:45:55.589 --> 1:45:57.299
No, thank you.

1:45:57.507 --> 1:46:00.047
- Ever?
- I hope not.

1:46:00.260 --> 1:46:01.720
Why not?

1:46:01.928 --> 1:46:04.718
Well, because some things are fun
the first time you do them...

1:46:04.931 --> 1:46:07.271
...and then not so much the next.

1:46:07.517 --> 1:46:10.347
- Like the bus?
- Yeah, like the bus.

1:46:10.604 --> 1:46:14.024
<i>I'm sorry. Guess I shouldn't laugh,</i>
<i>should I?</i>

1:46:14.274 --> 1:46:17.614
<i>It's promised in the Bible.</i>
<i>Pa says we'll find it some day.</i>

1:46:17.861 --> 1:46:20.201
<i>He doesn't know where it is, though.</i>

1:46:21.114 --> 1:46:24.334
<i>Didn't you ever want to have a home</i>
<i>of your own like other people?</i>

1:46:24.534 --> 1:46:26.374
<i>Sure.</i>

1:46:26.786 --> 1:46:28.866
<i>Sometimes when we're moving</i>
<i>at night...</i>

1:46:29.122 --> 1:46:32.252
<i>... we pass houses with lights</i>
<i>and people.</i>

1:46:32.459 --> 1:46:35.209
<i>Sometimes you can</i>
<i>hear them laughing...</i>

1:46:39.466 --> 1:46:42.836
<i>The next day, after work...</i>

1:46:43.053 --> 1:46:45.263
<i>... we just went to the beach.</i>

1:46:45.472 --> 1:46:47.352
<i>Far away from anything.</i>

1:46:47.557 --> 1:46:48.927
<i>Everything.</i>

1:46:49.142 --> 1:46:50.812
<i>Just Christopher and me.</i>

1:46:52.479 --> 1:46:54.809
- Did you see me?
- Yeah.

1:46:55.065 --> 1:46:58.105
<i>Far away from buses and noise...</i>

1:46:58.318 --> 1:47:03.948
<i>... and a constant disappointment</i>
<i>in my ten-gallon head...</i>

1:47:05.158 --> 1:47:06.988
<i>... and in myself.</i>

1:47:07.577 --> 1:47:09.957
- Chris, thank you very much.
- Well, thank you, Dean.

1:47:10.163 --> 1:47:12.003
- Take care.
- You made all the right moves.

1:47:12.249 --> 1:47:13.709
Thanks, Chris.

1:47:15.835 --> 1:47:17.125
<i>Because when I was young...</i>

1:47:17.337 --> 1:47:21.087
<i>... and I'd get an A on a history test</i>
<i>or whatever...</i>

1:47:21.341 --> 1:47:25.891
<i>... I'd get this good feeling about</i>
<i>all the things that I could be.</i>

1:47:27.847 --> 1:47:31.427
<i>And then I never became</i>
<i>any of them.</i>

1:47:38.942 --> 1:47:41.492
- Hey, Chris.
- Hey.

1:47:41.695 --> 1:47:44.315
- How you doing, Jay?
- I'm doing fine.

1:47:44.531 --> 1:47:48.661
Rumour has it you signed 31 accounts
for us from Pacific Bell.

1:47:48.869 --> 1:47:50.289
Yeah, yeah.

1:47:50.537 --> 1:47:54.287
Met some guys at a ball game,
got some cards. I've been working.

1:47:54.541 --> 1:47:56.131
I guess.

1:47:59.129 --> 1:48:01.339
So one more day.

1:48:01.548 --> 1:48:03.128
Getting nervous?

1:48:03.717 --> 1:48:06.087
- No, I'm okay.
- Yeah?

1:48:06.303 --> 1:48:08.223
Listen, whatever happens...

1:48:08.471 --> 1:48:10.851
...you've done a fantastic job, Chris.

1:48:11.057 --> 1:48:12.597
I mean that.

1:48:13.476 --> 1:48:15.266
Take care of yourself.

1:48:30.327 --> 1:48:33.457
Yes, Mr. Johnson.
Chris Gardner, Dean Witter.

1:48:33.830 --> 1:48:35.870
Yes, sir. Just calling
to thank you very much...

1:48:36.082 --> 1:48:38.592
...for your support
at last month's seminar.

1:48:39.169 --> 1:48:40.799
Yes, sir. Absolutely.

1:48:41.421 --> 1:48:43.051
Yes, sir.

1:48:43.256 --> 1:48:44.626
No, sir, that's it.

1:48:44.841 --> 1:48:47.301
Thank you very much. Bye-bye.

1:48:48.929 --> 1:48:51.809
Chris. Come.

1:49:19.209 --> 1:49:22.299
- Hi, Chris.
- Mr. Frohm, good to see you.

1:49:23.463 --> 1:49:25.343
- Nice shirt.
- Thank you, sir.

1:49:25.549 --> 1:49:26.759
- Chris.
- Hey, Jay.

1:49:27.217 --> 1:49:31.467
- Chris.
- Chris, sit down, please.

1:49:34.391 --> 1:49:38.481
I thought I'd wear a shirt today.

1:49:38.728 --> 1:49:40.648
You know,
being the last day and all.

1:49:40.897 --> 1:49:44.187
Well, thank you. Thank you.
We appreciate that.

1:49:45.068 --> 1:49:46.858
But...

1:49:47.070 --> 1:49:49.870
...wear one tomorrow though, okay?

1:49:50.073 --> 1:49:52.993
Because tomorrow's
going to be your first day...

1:49:53.743 --> 1:49:56.963
...if you'd like to work here
as a broker.

1:49:58.331 --> 1:50:00.131
Would you like that, Chris?

1:50:01.084 --> 1:50:02.634
Yes, sir.

1:50:02.836 --> 1:50:06.206
Good. We couldn't be happier.

1:50:07.173 --> 1:50:10.343
So welcome.

1:50:12.262 --> 1:50:17.232
- Was it as easy as it looked?
- No, sir. No, sir, it wasn't.

1:50:19.603 --> 1:50:21.943
- Good luck, Chris.
- Thank you. Thank you.

1:50:26.359 --> 1:50:28.029
Thank you, sir.

1:50:28.361 --> 1:50:30.241
Oh, Chris.

1:50:32.782 --> 1:50:34.832
I almost forgot.

1:50:36.870 --> 1:50:38.410
Thank you.

1:50:58.808 --> 1:51:01.018
<i>This part of my life...</i>

1:51:01.978 --> 1:51:04.108
<i>... this little part...</i>

1:51:07.484 --> 1:51:10.114
<i>... is called "Happiness."</i>

1:51:56.867 --> 1:52:00.447
Christopher. Christopher.
Come here.

1:52:30.150 --> 1:52:32.530
So how many...

1:52:32.736 --> 1:52:34.646
...planets are there?

1:52:35.989 --> 1:52:37.739
- Seven.
- Seven?

1:52:38.241 --> 1:52:40.081
Nine.

1:52:42.495 --> 1:52:44.535
Who's the king of the jungle?

1:52:44.915 --> 1:52:47.665
- Gorilla.
- The gorilla?

1:52:48.001 --> 1:52:49.381
The gorilla?

1:52:49.586 --> 1:52:51.206
No. Lion.

1:52:51.421 --> 1:52:54.051
Oh, yeah. Lion, lion, lion.

1:52:56.092 --> 1:52:59.102
Hey, Dad, listen to this.
Knock, knock.

1:52:59.346 --> 1:53:01.216
- Who's there?
- Shelby.

1:53:01.431 --> 1:53:02.561
Shelby who?

1:53:02.766 --> 1:53:06.556
<i>Shelby coming around the mountain</i>
<i>When she comes</i>

1:53:07.437 --> 1:53:08.727
- Knock knock.
- Who's there?

1:53:08.939 --> 1:53:11.399
- Nobody.
- Nobody who?

1:53:12.359 --> 1:53:14.069
Nobody who?

1:53:17.447 --> 1:53:20.367
Now, that's funny. I like that one.
